## 2.5.2 (Released 2025-01-05) {#2.5.2}

### Added overlay window support {#2.5.2-overlay-window}

<div class="changelog-entry">

You can now press <kbd>CTRL</kbd> + <kbd>ALT</kbd> + <kbd>N</kbd> to open an
overlay window of your selected [split](https://wiki.chatterino.com/Glossary/).

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/overlay-window.png", width=500, caption="Active overlay window over a stream") }}

{{ credit(author="nerixyz", helper="pajlada") }}

</div>

### Improved support for new Twitch features {#2.5.2-twitch-features}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Messages using the **Message Effects** or **Gigantify an Emote** power-up
feature are now highlighted. We don't actually show any message effects, nor do we gigantify the emote, but you can pretend the emote is bigger now that you know it's meant to be gigantified.

<div class="figure-group">
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/message-effect.png", width=400, caption="A <strong>Message Effect</strong> redemption") }}
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/gigantic-emote.png", width=400, caption="A <strong>Gigantify an Emote</strong> redemption") }}
</div>

Messages from Shared Chats now indicate which channel it was sent in.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/shared-chat.png", width=500, caption="A message from a shared chat") }}

We've provided better control of some AutoMod features. You can control whether or not to show AutoMod messages that were blocked due to a blocked term. By default, no blocked terms will be visible if you have streamer mode enabled.

<div class="figure-group">
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/automod-blocked-term-streamer-mode-enabled.png", width=400, caption="AutoMod alerts in streamer mode") }}
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/automod-blocked-term-streamer-mode-disabled.png", width=400, caption="AutoMod alerts with streamer mode disabled") }}
</div>

Added the `/warn` command which prevents the user from chatting until they acknowledge the warning on Twitch's website.

{{ credit(author="iProdigy, pajlada", helper="nerixyz") }}

</div>

### Added Twitch moderation features {#2.5.2-twitch-moderation}

<div class="changelog-entry">

If you use the inline moderation buttons, you can now upload custom icons for those buttons. This can be especially useful when you have a lot of them.

To add an icon to a moderation action, click Moderation in the Settings dialog, go to the Moderation buttons tab, and double-click the icon cell next to your action.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/moderation-button-settings.png", width=500, caption="Settings for custom moderation action buttons") }}

<div class="figure-group">
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/moderation-button-in-chat.png", width=300, caption="Custom moderation actions in chat") }}
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/moderation-button-after-click.png", width=300, caption="User timed out after clicking") }}
</div>

{{ credit(author="Mm2PL", helper="nerixyz, pajlada") }}

The `/ban`, `/timeout`, `/unban`, `/untimeout` commands now accept multiple channels if you want to easier wipe out cross-channel shenanigans.

Examples:

- Ban user in the chat you have selected: `/ban forsen`
- Ban user in a specific chat: `/ban --channel pajlada forsen`
- Ban user in two chat: `/ban --channel pajlada --channel nymn forsen`

Example command:

- Ban the user you right-clicked in the current channel + another channel: `/ban --channel {channel.name} --channel nymn {user.name}`

Example moderation button action:

- Ban the user in the current channel + another channel: `/ban --channel {channel.name} --channel nymn {user.name}`

{{ credit(author="pajlada") }}

</div>

### User Card Pronouns {#2.5.2-pronouns}

<div class="changelog-entry">

You can now show a user's pronoun from [pr.alejo.io](https://pr.alejo.io) in their User Card.

This feature can be enabled with the `Show user's pronouns in user card` setting.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/user-card-pronouns.png", width=400, caption="Pronouns shown in the user card") }}

{{ credit(author="franzitrone", helper="nerixyz, pajlada, iProdigy") }}

</div>

### Improved tab unread indicators {#2.5.2-tab-indicators}

<div class="changelog-entry">

If you have the same channel open in multiple tabs, "reading" the message in one tab marks the other tabs as unread.

{{ credit(author="hemirt", helper="nerixyz, pajlada") }}

</div>

### Plugins alpha release {#2.5.2-plugins}

<div class="changelog-entry">

We are testing a plugin system in Chatterino. Plugins are disabled by default.
To enable them, open the settings, go to `Plugins` and check the `Enable
plugins` checkbox.

Plugin documentation can be found in [the Chatterino2 repo](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/master/docs/wip-plugins.md).

The plugin system uses Lua with [sol2](https://github.com/ThePhD/sol2) by [ThePhD](https://github.com/ThePhD).

Got any ideas for what you'd like to be able to create with Plugins? Let us
know in [this discussion.](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/4999)

Have you started playing around with plugins and feel like something is
missing, or something is unergonomic? [Start a new discussion.](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/new?category=ideas)

Have questions about plugins? Ask in our <a href="{{ links.discord }}">Discord</a> or [start a new
discussion.](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/new?category=q-a)

{{ credit(author="Mm2PL", helper="nerixyz, pajlada") }}

</div>

### Improved high-DPI support on Windows {#2.5.2-high-dpi}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Text, buttons, windows should now better respect your Windows display scale setting. If you've previously increased your font size & Chatterino2 scale then you might need to re-adjust them with this release.

{{ credit(author="nerixyz") }}

</div>

### Duplicating tabs {#2.5.2-duplicate-tabs}

<div class="changelog-entry">

You can now duplicate tabs by right-clicking the tab and clicking "Duplicate
Tab".

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.2/duplicate-tab.webm", width=800, caption="Duplicating a tab, keeping filters & history intact") }}

{{ credit(author="KleberPF", helper="kornes, nerixyz, 8thony, pajlada") }}

</div>

### Modified tab visibility control {#2.5.2-tab-visibility}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Tab visibility control is now more verbose but hopefully easier to understand when right-clicking the tab bar.

This removes the default Ctrl+Shift+L hotkey which was used for toggling the "live only" tab visibility state. With there being more than two states, this caused more confusion than it helped.

Custom hotkeys can still be added to swap to various tab visibility modes.

{{ credit(author="pajlada", helper="nerixyz, Mm2PL") }}

</div>

### Improved error handling for Twitch API requests {#2.5.2-twitch-api-errors}

<div class="changelog-entry">

When using the `/settitle` and `/setgame` commands you're now told what's actually wrong.

{{ credit(author="JakeRYW") }}

</div>

### Updated browser list for "Open links in private mode" feature {#2.5.2-private-mode-browsers}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Added Brave, google-chrome-stable, firefox-devedition,
firefox-developer-edition, firefox-beta, and firefox-nightly as
supported browsers.

{{ credit(author="Niller2005, teknsl") }}

</div>

### Settings improvements {#2.5.2-settings-improvements}

<div class="changelog-entry">

- Dragging & dropping now shows a line indicator instead of rectangle while reordering entries in tables.
- Added some search tags for settings so it's easier to find them using search (e.g. "bttv" and "ffz" show all the BetterTTV and FrankerFaceZ settings.)

{{ credit(author="nerixyz, pajlada") }}

</div>

### Improved link handling {#2.5.2-link-parsing}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Prefixes and suffixes like parentheses around links are now recognized, and domain names are now checked, resulting in less false-positives.

{{ credit(author="nerixyz") }}

</div>

### Helix API emote loading {#2.5.2-helix-emotes}

<div class="changelog-entry">

We now use Twitch's Helix API to load the list of emotes you can post. This means we can now see most emotes you have access to, including event emotes.

{{ credit(author="nerixyz", helper="Felanbird, occluder, iProdigy, pajlada") }}

</div>

### Miscellaneous features {#2.5.2-miscellaneous-features}

<div class="changelog-entry">

- Chat popups now remember their last size. - Authored by @maliByatzes
- You can now use touchscreen gestures scroll in chat splits. - Authored by @camporter with help from @nerixyz @pajlada
- Made usernames clickable in more chat messages. - Authored by @jupjohn and @nerixyz with help from @pajlada
- Added the `--login <username>` CLI argument. This can be used to specify which account to start logged in as. - Authored by @lbrooney
- Initiating a reply will now show the message you're replying to, and the reply button has been made slightly prettier. - Authored by @dnsge and @nerixyz with help from @jupjohn and @pajlada
- Added `flags.action` filter variable, allowing you to filter on `/me` messages. - Authored by @Mm2PL
- Improved subscription & resubscription messages when they are multi-month subs. - Authored by @iProdigy
- Chat logs can now be organized by stream IDs rather than the current date. This makes it easier to log streams that consistently cross date boundaries. - Authored by @pajlada
- The size of the emote popup is now saved, and it now reloads Twitch emotes as they appear. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Added a setting to suppress live notifications on startup. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Added a warning before you block a channel, ensuring you're aware of the consequences. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Moderators can now see when users are warned or when raids are started/cancelled. - Authored by @iProdigy
- The window layout settings file is now backed up like your other settings, in case of an unfortunate event. - Authored by @nerixyz

</div>

