- Fixed message history occasionally not loading after a sleep. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed windows on Windows not saving correctly when snapping them to the edges. Authored by @nerixyz with help from @8thony
- Fixed user info card popups adding duplicate line to log files. - Authored by @pajlada
- Fixed tooltips and input completion popups not working after moving a split. - Authored by @pajlada and @nerixyz
- Fixed `/clearmessages` not working with more than one window. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed splits staying paused after unfocusing Chatterino in certain configurations. - Authored by @Mm2PL and @nerixyz
- Fixed account switch not being saved if no other settings were changed. - Authored by @pajlada
- Fixed a crash that could occur when handling the quick switcher popup really quickly. - Authored by @pajlada
- Fixed 7TV badges being inadvertently animated. - Authored by @pajlada
- Fixed some tooltips not being readable. - Authored by @pajlada
- Fixed log files being locked longer than needed. - Authored by @nerixyz with help from @kornes
- Fixed global badges not showing in anonymous mode. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed incorrect message being disabled in some cases upon approving or denying a message caught by AutoMod. - Authored by @iProdigy with help from @jupjohn
- Fixed emotes starting with ":" not tab-completing. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed 7TV emotes and usernames messing with Qt's HTML. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed incorrect messages getting replaced visually. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed pause indicator not appearing in certain cases. - Authored by @nerixyz
- Fixed usercards not showing the login name in specific cases. - Authored by @Mm2PL
- Fixed BTTV emotes occasionally showing the wrong author. - Authored by @nerixyz

</div>

### Nerdier things {#2.5.2-nerd-things}

<div class="changelog-entry">

This release will be the last release of Chatterino2 that supports Qt5, meaning Windows 7 will disappear. Please update your Windows system if you're still on Windows 7.

The IRC beta feature has been removed.

A huge effort has been taken to refactor our message building process, adding a bunch of tests to them to ensuring it will take a lot more effort for us to break message building going forward. - Authored by @nerixyz with help from @pajlada

</div>
